= Peer review — Technical =

Peer review is a human evaluation process operating under incomplete information and finite time. Its reliability depends on reviewer selection, expertise, incentives, conflicts of interest, editorial procedures, transparency, and the criteria being evaluated. Different review models trade off anonymity, accountability, speed, and openness.

== Modeling / implementation cautions ==
* peer review ≠ proof of correctness
* peer review ≠ replication
* peer-reviewed ≠ error-free

== References ==
* National Research Council, ''Peer Review in the Department of Energy—Office of Science and Technology'' (1997), definition of peer review.
* Committee on Publication Ethics (COPE), peer-review guidance and ethical guidelines.
* UNESCO, ''Recommendation on Open Science'' (2021), peer review within scientific knowledge creation and evaluation.
